+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## Intent
+Build a TodoMVC app per `assets/app-spec.md`, vanilla JS, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence, using `assets/app-template.index.html` as the base markup.
+
+## What was authored
+- `features/todo-core.feature` — 21 scenarios: CRUD, toggle, delete, counter, clear-completed, editing, empty state
+- `features/routing.feature` — 8 scenarios: all/active/completed routes, filter toggle, filter persistence
+- `features/persistence.feature` — 4 scenarios: localStorage round-trip, key format, non-persisted editing, clear
+- `watchbill.json` — 7 watches ordering QM through the implementation
+
+## Next
+- Dispatch QM against the watchbill. The feature steps reference DOM interactions; QM will need happy-dom (installed) and step defs.
+- Template index.html lives at `assets/app-template.index.html` — QM will copy it to `index.html` as part of work.
+- `css/app.css` directory created and ready for overrides.
+- `js/` directory created for app code.
+- todomvc-common and todomvc-app-css are now installed.
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3e8f0c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+Feature: localStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that my list is preserved between sessions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Save and restore todo state
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist after page reload
+    Given I create a todo "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo "Walk dog"
+    And I mark "Walk dog" as completed
+    When I reload the page
+    Then I see 2 todos in the list
+    And "Walk dog" has class "completed"
+    And "Buy milk" does not have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: localStorage uses correct key and format
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a key matching "todos-"
+    And the stored value is valid JSON with objects having keys "id", "title", "completed"
+
+  Rule: Editing mode is not persisted
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    And I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the page
+    Then "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Rule: Empty state after clear
+
+  Scenario: localStorage clears when all todos are deleted
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    When I delete "Buy milk"
+    Then the localStorage key is empty or absent
\ No newline at end of file
